WEBVTT

00:05.330 --> 00:07.540
What the hell were you guys thinking?!

00:07.630 --> 00:10.800
We tried to stop her, but...!

00:10.880 --> 00:13.590
They're safe now. Isn't that all that matters?

00:16.680 --> 00:20.720
They were victims in the attack, and
there hadn't been any rescue operations!

00:21.390 --> 00:24.270
Don't underestimate the GGP!

00:24.350 --> 00:26.770
Club activities are canceled for now!

00:26.860 --> 00:31.110
Everyone forget this ever happened! Don't tell anyone.

00:31.190 --> 00:33.740
I'll dispose of this.

00:35.570 --> 00:41.450
<i>Why is he so flustered?</i>
<i>He really fears the GGP and police...</i>

00:42.370 --> 00:46.620
<i>Is the Fuego what's agitating him? Or could it be...?</i>

02:37.740 --> 02:41.490
Welcome back. How'd the police announcement go?

02:41.570 --> 02:45.120
"No comment" to everything. A huge waste of time.

02:45.200 --> 02:47.370
Well, there is a news blackout and all.

02:47.450 --> 02:49.370
They said they were gonna respond next time

02:49.460 --> 02:52.210
with some anti-terrorism countermeasure or whatever...

02:52.290 --> 02:54.960
That's fine, just don't hold press
conferences in the middle of the night!

02:55.050 --> 02:57.920
I got a good haul here, though!

03:00.470 --> 03:03.510
A girl?! Girls ride these too?

03:08.560 --> 03:11.350
This year's national championship winner.

03:11.440 --> 03:13.900
Tamayo Kataoka, a.k.a. the RideBack Princess.

03:13.980 --> 03:15.900
Age 22 and a college student.

03:15.980 --> 03:18.860
Her father is Nanpu Kataoka,
a top member of the leading party,

03:18.940 --> 03:21.820
and her brother is
a high-ranking Police Agency official.

03:21.910 --> 03:25.070
That would explain the media blackout...

03:25.160 --> 03:28.120
And the machine that jumped was likely a Type L Fuego

03:28.200 --> 03:30.290
manufactured by Teryan Kaduro.

03:30.370 --> 03:35.960
According to dealers, there are
probably only twenty or so in the country.

03:36.040 --> 03:39.460
Write up a report and mail it to me.

03:39.550 --> 03:41.090
Are you going out to do research?

03:41.170 --> 03:44.550
Good work, Sato. Now get some sleep.

03:47.310 --> 03:51.270
<i>The girl who broke through</i>
<i>the GGP security net on a RideBack</i>

03:51.350 --> 03:54.690
<i>is related to a politician and a police official...</i>

03:54.770 --> 03:56.810
<i>This is gonna be a huge story...!</i>

04:15.210 --> 04:17.080
Now for the six o'clock news.

04:17.170 --> 04:24.010
Yesterday's takeover of the TV Tower
by anti-GGP terrorist group BMA

04:24.090 --> 04:30.560
affected citizens in surrounding buildings,
leaving 7 dead and 167 injured,

04:30.640 --> 04:35.600
making it the worst
anti-GGP terrorist attack this year.

04:36.520 --> 04:40.690
In response, the government held
an emergency ministry meeting last night

04:40.780 --> 04:44.110
and announced plans to create an agency combining

04:44.200 --> 04:48.120
anti-terrorism committee members
of the MIAC and IBA with the GGP

04:48.200 --> 04:52.160
in order to further increase
readiness for terrorist attacks.

04:53.370 --> 04:55.390
There's nothing about us...

05:10.680 --> 05:11.160
Brother

05:23.690 --> 05:27.070
--Do you know what time it--?!
--You're awake?

05:27.160 --> 05:30.910
Women hate men who call whenever they please.

05:30.990 --> 05:32.950
Anything out of the ordinary?

05:35.250 --> 05:38.170
I already told you I'd call if anything happens.

05:38.250 --> 05:39.790
Sorry.

05:39.880 --> 05:43.170
--Say, have you seen the news?
--The TV Tower attack?

05:43.260 --> 05:45.170
We have information that a civilian girl

05:45.260 --> 05:48.050
was riding the RideBack
that broke through the security net.

05:48.140 --> 05:52.430
So? There are lots of women who ride RideBacks.

05:52.510 --> 05:55.850
You don't have anything to do with this, do you?

05:55.930 --> 05:58.640
You suspect your own sister?! You're pathetic!

05:58.730 --> 05:59.810
Hey!

06:04.440 --> 06:09.450
Participated as a volunteer soldier
in the GGP army during the war.

06:09.530 --> 06:12.120
Helped found the RideBack squad.

06:12.200 --> 06:16.580
Achieved great results as
a guerrilla warfare specialist

06:16.660 --> 06:20.920
and returned to Japan in 2026
after an honorable discharge.

06:21.000 --> 06:24.050
<i>This is the hero Romanov spoke of...?</i>

06:29.300 --> 06:31.930
RideBack club, huh?

06:34.720 --> 06:39.020
Man, Okakura is acting way too jittery.

06:39.100 --> 06:41.560
Yeah. That wasn't like him at all.

06:42.110 --> 06:44.690
It was almost like he was blaming us!

06:47.610 --> 06:51.530
Come to think of it, wasn't it
Okakura who started this club?

06:51.620 --> 06:56.240
Yeah. Kataoka and I had just enrolled,
so I guess it was three years ago...

06:56.330 --> 06:59.960
Okakura hasn't been in a single race, has he?

07:00.040 --> 07:01.830
I think he prefers the mechanic stuff.

07:01.920 --> 07:05.420
I bet he's a real chicken despite how he looks...

07:05.500 --> 07:10.090
No way. His riding technique is really something.

07:10.180 --> 07:13.760
He probably knows more about
RideBacks than anyone else in Japan!

07:13.850 --> 07:17.140
He's respected by
RideBack people throughout the country, too!

07:18.430 --> 07:21.020
Rin! Good morning!

07:21.100 --> 07:22.100
Good morning.

07:22.190 --> 07:23.350
You okay?

07:23.440 --> 07:25.610
Yes, I've calmed down.

07:30.240 --> 07:31.280
Umm...

07:31.360 --> 07:34.070
Yeah, the Fuego's gone.

07:34.160 --> 07:37.280
Okakura hauled it off after we left yesterday.

07:37.370 --> 07:38.450
Do you mean he...?!

07:38.540 --> 07:41.580
I don't think he's dismantled it yet, though.

07:42.750 --> 07:45.040
Is Shoko all right?

07:45.130 --> 07:47.290
She still doesn't seem well...

07:47.380 --> 07:49.630
I can't blame her; it's still so recent.

07:49.710 --> 07:52.380
Plus, she was caught in the middle of it all...

07:52.470 --> 07:54.470
I'm worried.

07:54.550 --> 07:57.970
I know! Why don't we all go and visit her?

07:58.060 --> 08:01.180
No, I think a commotion would make it worse...

08:01.270 --> 08:06.440
That's right. A delicate maiden's heart
should be watched over gently.

08:07.190 --> 08:09.650
Well, since we won't see each other for a while,

08:09.730 --> 08:12.280
let's go out to celebrate
the canceling of club activities!

08:12.360 --> 08:14.110
Yeah! It's been a while!

08:14.200 --> 08:16.530
We'll be hungry when we're done cleaning up, too!

08:16.620 --> 08:19.700
Hurray! It feels like we're a clique!

08:19.790 --> 08:22.660
We're not a clique! We're a bonafide club!

08:23.580 --> 08:25.460
Excuse me!

08:25.540 --> 08:29.670
Is Tamayo Kataoka, the RideBack Princess, here?

08:30.630 --> 08:32.670
Umm, who might you be?

08:35.340 --> 08:36.930
Here's my card.

08:41.560 --> 08:43.980
You're a freelance writer?

08:46.020 --> 08:47.560
Thanks!

08:49.770 --> 08:54.490
Are you sure about this?! I think
she's looking into yesterday's incident!

08:54.570 --> 08:59.450
Yeah, maybe so, but Tamayo wasn't there

08:59.530 --> 09:02.240
and being under suspicion
wouldn't be a big deal to her.

09:02.330 --> 09:04.250
That makes some sense!

09:04.330 --> 09:08.540
I just sent her a text about it and about our party.

09:08.630 --> 09:11.300
Is Okakura in the lab?

09:11.380 --> 09:13.300
Umm...

09:13.380 --> 09:15.090
I'll go check.

09:18.850 --> 09:20.470
Leave your message at the tone.

09:22.100 --> 09:25.730
Hello? Shoko? How are you feeling?

09:26.900 --> 09:30.560
I was invited to go eat with everyone.

09:30.650 --> 09:33.530
I thought maybe you'd like to come, too...

09:35.990 --> 09:37.570
I'll call again later.

09:54.260 --> 09:55.380
What do you want?

09:57.590 --> 10:01.300
Umm, we're all going out to eat, so...

10:01.390 --> 10:03.850
I told you to stay put!

10:11.110 --> 10:12.150
What?

10:13.360 --> 10:16.690
Umm... Where's the Fuego?

10:16.780 --> 10:19.070
I dismantled and destroyed it.

10:23.790 --> 10:25.790
If you're done, then leave.

10:28.540 --> 10:32.790
Are Fuegos a special kind of RideBack...?

10:35.170 --> 10:37.630
Who told you that? Hishida?

10:41.890 --> 10:43.430
Found ya!

10:46.810 --> 10:48.890
You're Tamayo Kataoka, right?

10:50.480 --> 10:53.110
I'm Yoda. I'm a freelance journalist.

10:53.190 --> 10:55.690
I have three questions I'd like to ask.

10:55.780 --> 10:57.570
What are your thoughts on the RideBack

10:57.650 --> 11:00.030
that broke through the security checkpoints yesterday?

11:01.820 --> 11:06.700
Then how about the fact that
a girl was riding that RideBack?

11:06.790 --> 11:08.750
--A girl?!
--Yes!

11:10.460 --> 11:13.000
It's nothing special. There are lots of female riders.

11:13.080 --> 11:16.050
Did your police official brother say that?

11:17.010 --> 11:18.380
Are you picking a fight?

11:18.470 --> 11:23.180
No, not at all! Not with
the daughter of such an important man!

11:34.190 --> 11:36.770
She isn't quite what I expected...

11:39.900 --> 11:45.870
During the incident, someone
showed up and helped us escape...

11:47.330 --> 11:54.500
I... didn't understand what he was saying...

11:56.960 --> 12:01.510
Ogata. The GGP and police haven't announced anything,

12:01.590 --> 12:04.220
but they did get you on film.

12:05.430 --> 12:08.720
I know you're tense, but all we can
do is wait for them to make a move.

12:08.810 --> 12:12.020
--We didn't do anything wrong--
--I know!

12:15.610 --> 12:19.980
I'm responsible for this. I'll protect you.

12:21.820 --> 12:23.450
Now go.

12:45.010 --> 12:52.250
I'm sorry, Rin. I can't.
Go have fun. I'll be fine.

13:05.570 --> 13:06.860
Heya!

13:07.410 --> 13:10.080
Did you see the news yesterday, Kenji?!

13:10.160 --> 13:14.160
Yeah, I saw! I think it was an off-road Teryan Kaduro!

13:14.250 --> 13:16.540
You sure know your stuff, RideBack Geek!

13:16.620 --> 13:17.670
You can count on me!

13:17.750 --> 13:20.710
It sure put the GGP in its place!

13:20.800 --> 13:23.130
I totally wanna ride a RideBack now!

13:23.210 --> 13:27.300
Forget it. You could never make a jump like that.

13:28.220 --> 13:30.300
Hey, guys. Long time, no see.

13:30.390 --> 13:33.270
--Oh, Kizaki!
--Good to see you!

13:33.350 --> 13:36.100
Heya, Kenji. You seem well.

13:36.190 --> 13:37.850
Yeah, I guess...

13:37.940 --> 13:40.110
Huh. That's a lukewarm reply.

13:40.190 --> 13:43.940
I was just thinking of giving you a call, actually.

13:44.030 --> 13:45.440
What for?

13:45.530 --> 13:51.030
Well, there's a meeting coming
up soon, but we need more people...

13:53.540 --> 13:54.750
Really?!

13:54.830 --> 13:57.120
I figured you'd jump at the chance.

13:57.210 --> 13:59.170
Absolutely! Please!

14:02.670 --> 14:06.380
I see. Yes. I understand.

14:07.510 --> 14:10.010
Okakura and Tamayo can't make it.

14:10.090 --> 14:13.350
Ma'am! Knock two people off the list!

14:13.430 --> 14:15.600
This isn't much of a gathering now.

14:15.680 --> 14:17.730
Kawai still isn't here.

14:17.810 --> 14:19.850
Maybe we should just start anyway.

14:19.940 --> 14:21.520
I agree!

14:21.610 --> 14:22.690
All right...!

14:22.770 --> 14:24.650
Cheers!

14:24.730 --> 14:26.320
Umm...

14:28.240 --> 14:31.370
A terrorist uproar just when he's appointed...

14:31.450 --> 14:35.910
And an ex-mercenary RideBack
specialist he had Public Security watch...

14:37.120 --> 14:38.790
Is it coincidence?

14:43.630 --> 14:46.630
Is this a fixed game? Or could it be...?

14:52.100 --> 14:54.140
Sorry to trouble you at a busy time.

14:54.220 --> 14:55.600
It's no problem.

14:55.680 --> 14:59.770
Unsightly video of the RideBack
breaking through GGP security

14:59.850 --> 15:03.110
has been aired all over the country,

15:03.190 --> 15:07.320
but it has only bolstered support
for the introduction of police RideBacks.

15:08.400 --> 15:10.740
I doubt you find that amusing, though.

15:12.240 --> 15:15.990
If things go smoothly,
test deployments will begin early next month.

15:16.080 --> 15:20.120
Has the GGP not disclosed
anything about the RideBack suspect

15:20.210 --> 15:24.670
because you want
the terrorists to remain a latent threat?

15:24.750 --> 15:30.170
I will turn it over to you eventually.
I just have a personal interest in it.

15:30.260 --> 15:34.390
I'm curious to know what sort
of person can pull off such acrobatics.

15:39.270 --> 15:42.230
Images from an armored vehicle's camera.

15:46.690 --> 15:50.280
What? Rin left?

15:50.360 --> 15:52.280
She was worried about Shoko.

15:52.360 --> 15:54.700
Rin certainly is nice.

15:54.780 --> 15:57.870
It's kind of lonely, but shall we eat?

15:57.950 --> 16:01.250
Count me in! I'm starving!

16:04.040 --> 16:06.500
The ham cutlets here are always great!

16:06.590 --> 16:07.840
Do you come often?

16:07.920 --> 16:11.170
Yeah. We often spend all night
on our machines before a race

16:11.260 --> 16:13.430
and eat here on our way home.

16:13.510 --> 16:16.300
It's like a page out of adolescence.

16:16.390 --> 16:18.760
Hey! That's mine!

16:19.390 --> 16:23.480
--It's no big deal! Just order more!
--No! I just was about to eat it!

16:25.020 --> 16:28.230
Now what's your problem?! I'm paying for this!

16:28.320 --> 16:34.860
--terrorist aboard the RideBack
has been caught on film.

16:34.950 --> 16:37.370
The GGP and police department have yet

16:37.450 --> 16:41.120
to make any official statements about this individual.

16:41.200 --> 16:44.120
Our program happened to record video

16:44.210 --> 16:47.710
of the fleeing individual from a different angle,

16:47.790 --> 16:50.460
but due to the possibility of being a terrorist,

16:50.550 --> 16:55.260
our station was advised not to air it.

16:55.340 --> 16:58.430
However, after detailed analysis
of the image by a specialist,

16:58.510 --> 17:03.680
we now believe this person is not a terrorist,

17:03.770 --> 17:08.230
but rather an ordinary citizen caught in the incident.

17:11.480 --> 17:12.940
Rin Ogata.

17:13.950 --> 17:16.950
The target has been under
Intelligence Agency surveillance

17:17.030 --> 17:19.320
for the past 18 hours.

17:19.410 --> 17:22.620
It is now clear that
the rider of this robotic motorcycle

17:22.700 --> 17:24.620
who broke through the GGP security net

17:24.710 --> 17:29.840
is neither soldier nor terrorist,
but rather an ordinary girl!

17:32.590 --> 17:33.110
We called the party off. Let's eat together. -Rin

17:40.680 --> 17:44.140
First, let's take a look at this shocking footage.

17:45.890 --> 17:49.940
So, Mr. Suzuki, what are
your thoughts of this footage?

17:50.020 --> 17:55.900
Rumors from eyewitnesses and online
said it might have been a woman,

17:55.990 --> 17:58.610
but now it's been proven clearly.

17:58.700 --> 18:01.830
What's more, there's someone else with her.

18:01.910 --> 18:05.410
I believe they may have been
citizens who escaped together.

18:05.500 --> 18:10.580
Is it really possible to break
through a GGP security net on a RideBack?

18:10.670 --> 18:15.300
I would like to say it's impossible,
but given that it's actually happened...

18:15.380 --> 18:19.970
I'm honestly surprised that
there exists such an agile machine.

18:20.050 --> 18:26.480
Are you saying it's a rather
special type of RideBack then?

18:26.560 --> 18:28.350
I hear that the police are close

18:28.440 --> 18:31.900
to officially adopting them
for counter-terrorism purposes;

18:31.980 --> 18:35.110
do you think that has
anything to do with this incident?

18:35.190 --> 18:40.240
It's a wholly different type than
the special counter-terrorist "White Rides"

18:40.320 --> 18:43.910
and is also unlike the RideBacks
witnessed in the terrorist attacks.

18:43.990 --> 18:46.950
It's based on a market model intended for enthusiasts,

18:47.040 --> 18:49.620
so I believe there's no connection.

18:49.710 --> 18:53.590
What kind of vehicle is a RideBack in the first place?

18:53.670 --> 19:00.130
I suppose it's easiest to describe
them as a motorcycle-robot hybrid.

19:02.050 --> 19:03.510
A girl like this?

19:03.600 --> 19:07.350
I don't know who taught her in secret,

19:07.430 --> 19:11.350
but a civilian girl broke
through the military's security net.

19:11.440 --> 19:14.820
Despite your hate for them,
RideBacks are quite impressive.

19:16.530 --> 19:18.570
Colonel. It's time.

19:23.450 --> 19:29.620
Oh, yes. I hear your sister
won the championship the other day.

19:29.710 --> 19:31.410
Why did you hide that?

19:31.500 --> 19:34.540
I didn't think it was necessary to report.

19:34.630 --> 19:37.710
For an amateur, she's quite skilled.

19:37.800 --> 19:41.170
Was it your sister who
introduced this girl to RideBacks?

19:43.930 --> 19:45.970
I take it there's nothing else?

19:46.060 --> 19:48.720
It won't do you any good to hide anything.

19:55.690 --> 19:57.400
That will be all.

19:59.360 --> 20:03.150
I'll send copies of
these documents to you at a later date.

20:15.880 --> 20:20.260
Let's take another look at the footage
of the mysterious RideBack girl.

20:32.810 --> 20:36.520
The mysterious RideBack girl...

20:44.950 --> 20:46.740
<i>I'm crazy.</i>

20:47.700 --> 20:49.660
<i>Why did I do that?</i>

20:51.120 --> 20:53.910
<i>Because I was so focused on saving Shoko...?</i>

20:56.540 --> 21:01.420
<i>No. Some part of me enjoyed that sense of fear.</i>

21:08.180 --> 21:10.850
<i>What's happened to me?</i>

21:22.320 --> 21:25.740
This body won't be able to keep up with our movements.

21:25.820 --> 21:30.660
No, a titanium frame with reinforced
stainless steel would be pretty light.

21:30.740 --> 21:34.250
Where would the heavy ordnance be loaded then?

21:34.330 --> 21:35.790
That's the thing...

21:37.540 --> 21:39.830
What do you think?

21:39.920 --> 21:43.420
Simply strengthening a machine
doesn't make it more of a threat.

21:43.510 --> 21:48.720
What's vital to victory on
the battlefield is the ability to "leap" freely.

21:48.800 --> 21:53.770
We're going to teach them
how RideBacks really fight...

21:56.730 --> 22:01.310
Even when he laughs

22:03.400 --> 22:08.950
I'm thinking of you before I realize it

22:12.030 --> 22:16.910
And the hands holding his

22:18.830 --> 22:24.250
feel your warmth, too

22:26.470 --> 22:30.220
Even if I cut out my recollections

22:30.300 --> 22:34.180
and drive them out of my heart

22:34.270 --> 22:37.930
or try to kick the memories out

22:38.020 --> 22:42.400
I still think of you

22:42.480 --> 22:46.900
Time now passes and seasons fly by

22:46.990 --> 22:50.740
Even if that smile starts to become hazy

22:50.820 --> 22:54.740
my heart will never forget you

22:54.830 --> 22:58.500
(even if we can never meet again)

22:58.580 --> 23:02.330
Even if I knock over photos of us smiling

23:02.420 --> 23:06.630
or try to hide my overflowing feelings

23:07.720 --> 23:10.880
my heart will never forget

23:11.680 --> 23:14.930
my memories with you

23:26.030 --> 23:41.020
New Hishida Theatre

23:27.280 --> 23:30.450
Don't worry, Rin! They reported
about you, but you'll be all right!

23:30.530 --> 23:32.910
You were just a victim in the incident anyway!

23:32.990 --> 23:36.410
We'll-- no-- I'll protect you!

23:35.870 --> 23:39.560
Next Episode:

23:35.870 --> 23:39.560
The Lightning-Fast RideBack

23:36.500 --> 23:38.540
Rin left, you know.

23:38.620 --> 23:40.420
Oh, yeah...
